---
import MainLayout from "../layouts/mainLayout.astro";
import MainSuperTextCitation from "../components/mainSuperTextCitation.astro";

import "../styles/global.css";
---

<MainLayout metaTitle="Test">
    <main class="bg-mainBrand text-secondaryBrand max-w-1080 mx-auto">
        <h1>Test</h1>
        <ul class="mt-30 pb-30 gap-50 flex flex-col lg:max-w-1080 lg:mx-auto">
            <li
                class="flex lg:w-full lg:flex-nowrap lg:p-0 text-secondaryBrand"
                data-accName="case-study-1"
            >
                <div
                    class="text-bodyCopy flex flex-col gap-30 lg:flex-row lg:flex-wrap"
                >
                    <div
                        class="flex flex-col gap-30 lg:flex-row lg:flex-nowrap lg:items-start lg:overflow-hidden"
                    >
                        <div class="lg:w-2/3 lg:min-h-300">
                            <h3 class="text-bodyHead font-bold mb-20">
                                How loot boxes stole a teen's savings
                            </h3>
                            <div>
                                <p id="citation-1-reference">
                                    When Johnathon opened his first FIFA pack at
                                    the age of 12, he didn't know he was
                                    gambling. FIFA pack's, also known as loot
                                    boxes, offer a small chance to play his
                                    favorite players in-game for real world
                                    money.<MainSuperTextCitation
                                        citationNumber="1"
                                        citationLink="https://doi.org/10.1016/j.addbeh.2022.107327"
                                        citationText="Spicer, S. G., Fullwood, C., Close, J., Nicklin, L. L., Lloyd, J., & Lloyd, H. (2022). Loot boxes and problem gambling: Investigating the 'Gateway hypothesis.' Addictive Behaviors, 131, 107327."
                                    /> By purchasing them, he was simulating the highs
                                    and lows of real world gambling. The mechanics
                                    of loot boxes are psychological similar to gambling,
                                    and can led vulnerable players like Johnathon
                                    to problem spending-- "...I was addicted to the
                                    buzz of chance when I bought packs."<MainSuperTextCitation
                                    citationNumber="2"
                                    citationLink="https://doi.org/10.1016/j.addbeh.2022.107327"
                                    citationText="Spicer, S. G., Fullwood, C., Close, J., Nicklin, L. L., Lloyd, J., & Lloyd, H. (2022). Loot boxes and problem gambling: Investigating the 'Gateway hypothesis.' Addictive Behaviors, 131, 107327."
                                />
                                </p>
                            </div>
                        </div>

                        <div
                            class="relative self-stretch lg:w-1/3 overflow-hidden"
                        >
                            <img
                                class="max-h-[40vh] lg:absolute lg:inset-0 w-full lg:h-full object-cover"
                                src="https://placehold.co/350x330"
                                alt=""
                            />
                        </div>
                    </div>
                    <div>
                        <h4 class="text-bodySubHead font-bold mb-10">
                            Solutions
                        </h4>
                        <p class="mb-20">
                            Johnathon is not alone. As long as games like FIFA
                            employ exploitative monetization methods, stories
                            like his will continue. The following changes can
                            help make games safer for kids to enjoy:
                        </p>
                        <ul class="list-disc list-inside mb-20">
                            <li>Get loot boxes labeled for R-18 only</li>
                            <li>Add daily spending limit caps</li>
                            <li>Enable easily accessible spending logs</li>
                        </ul>
                        <p class="mb-30">
                            <a
                                href="https://www.bbc.com/news/business-53337020"
                                class="text-secondaryBrand underline"
                                >View the full article on Jonathan's story on
                                the BBC<svg
                                    class="inline-block mb-10 ml-1"
                                    width="20px"
                                    height="20px"
                                    viewBox="0 0 24 24"
                                    style="cursor:pointer"
                                    ><g
                                        stroke-width="2.1"
                                        stroke="#fffafa"
                                        fill="none"
                                        stroke-linecap="round"
                                        stroke-linejoin="round"
                                        ><polyline
                                            points="17 13.5 17 19.5 5 19.5 5 7.5 11 7.5"
                                        ></polyline><path
                                            d="M14,4.5 L20,4.5 L20,10.5 M20,4.5 L11,13.5"
                                        ></path></g
                                    ></svg
                                ></a
                            >
                        </p>
                    </div>
                </div>
            </li>
            <li
                class="flex lg:w-full lg:flex-nowrap lg:p-0 text-secondaryBrand"
                data-accName="case-study-1"
            >
                <div
                    class="text-bodyCopy flex flex-col gap-30 lg:flex-row lg:flex-wrap"
                >
                    <div
                        class="flex flex-col gap-30 lg:flex-row lg:flex-nowrap lg:items-start lg:overflow-hidden"
                    >
                        <div class="lg:w-2/3 lg:min-h-300">
                            <h3 class="text-bodyHead font-bold mb-20">
                                How loot boxes stole a teen's savings
                            </h3>
                            <div>
                                <p>
                                    When Johnathon opened his first FIFA pack at
                                    the age of 12, he didn't know he was
                                    gambling. FIFA pack's, also known as loot
                                    boxes, offer a small chance to play his
                                    favorite players in-game for real world
                                    money. By purchasing them, he was simulating
                                    the highs and lows of real world gambling.
                                    The mechanics of loot boxes are
                                    psychological similar to gambling, and can
                                    led vulnerable players like Johnathon to
                                    problem spending-- "...I was addicted to the
                                    buzz of chance when I bought packs."
                                </p>

                                <div
                                    class="relative self-stretch lg:w-1/3 overflow-hidden"
                                >
                                    <img
                                        class="max-h-[40vh] lg:absolute lg:inset-0 w-full lg:h-full object-cover"
                                        src="https://placehold.co/350x330"
                                        alt=""
                                    />
                                </div>
                            </div>
                            <div>
                                <h4 class="text-bodySubHead font-bold mb-10">
                                    Solutions
                                </h4>
                                <p class="mb-20">
                                    Johnathon is not alone. As long as games
                                    like FIFA employ exploitative monetization
                                    methods, stories like his will continue. The
                                    following changes can help make games safer
                                    for kids to enjoy:
                                </p>
                                <ul class="list-disc list-inside mb-20">
                                    <li>
                                        Get loot boxes labeled for R-18 only
                                    </li>
                                    <li>Add daily spending limit caps</li>
                                    <li>
                                        Enable easily accessible spending logs
                                    </li>
                                </ul>
                                <p class="mb-30">
                                    <a
                                        href="https://www.bbc.com/news/business-53337020"
                                        class="text-secondaryBrand underline"
                                        >View the full article on Jonathan's
                                        story on the BBC<svg
                                            class="inline-block mb-10 ml-1"
                                            width="20px"
                                            height="20px"
                                            viewBox="0 0 24 24"
                                            style="cursor:pointer"
                                            ><g
                                                stroke-width="2.1"
                                                stroke="#fffafa"
                                                fill="none"
                                                stroke-linecap="round"
                                                stroke-linejoin="round"
                                                ><polyline
                                                    points="17 13.5 17 19.5 5 19.5 5 7.5 11 7.5"
                                                ></polyline><path
                                                    d="M14,4.5 L20,4.5 L20,10.5 M20,4.5 L11,13.5"
                                                ></path></g
                                            ></svg
                                        ></a
                                    >
                                </p>
                            </div>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                    <li
                        class="flex lg:w-full lg:flex-nowrap lg:p-0 text-secondaryBrand"
                        data-accName="case-study-2"
                    >
                        <div
                            class="text-bodyCopy flex flex-col gap-30 lg:flex-row lg:flex-wrap"
                        >
                            <div
                                class="flex flex-col gap-30 lg:flex-row lg:flex-nowrap lg:items-start lg:overflow-hidden"
                            >
                                <div class="lg:w-2/3 lg:min-h-300">
                                    <h3 class="text-bodyHead font-bold mb-15">
                                        A 10-year-old daughter fell victim to
                                        aggressive monetization
                                    </h3>

                                    <p class="">
                                        Georgina thought her daughter's Roblox
                                        account was compromised by hackers when
                                        she saw the bill. Her 10-year-old child
                                        spent over "£2,500 on the [Roblox]"
                                        through £20 microtransactions. Despite
                                        the claim of unauthorized purchases,
                                        Georgina's requests for refunds from
                                        both Roblox and her bank, Tesco, were
                                        initially denied. Only after the BBC
                                        shared the story did they refund her.
                                    </p>
                                </div>

                                <div
                                    class="relative self-stretch lg:w-1/3 overflow-hidden"
                                >
                                    <img
                                        class="max-h-[40vh] lg:absolute lg:inset-0 w-full lg:h-full object-cover"
                                        src="https://placehold.co/350x330"
                                        alt=""
                                    />
                                </div>
                            </div>
                            <div>
                                <h4 class="text-bodySubHead font-bold mb-10">
                                    Solutions
                                </h4>
                                <p class="mb-20">
                                    Georgina is not the only parent with the rug
                                    pulled from beneath her, yet it is not her
                                    fault nor the fault of her daughter. We must
                                    examine and criticize the systems in place
                                    that allowed a 10-year-old child to spend
                                    over £2,500 in a month. To prevent more
                                    stories like Georgina's, we can advocate for
                                    the following:
                                </p>
                                <ul class="list-disc list-inside mb-20">
                                    <li>
                                        Default spending limit caps on all kids
                                        games
                                    </li>
                                    <li>
                                        Free and public education on online
                                        safety for both children and parents
                                    </li>
                                    <li>
                                        Consumer's right to refunds for digital
                                        product purchases
                                    </li>
                                </ul>
                            </div>
                        </div>
                    </li>
                </div>
            </li>
        </ul>
    </main>

    <script>
        const citationPopupContainers = document.getElementsByClassName(
            "citationPopupContainers",
        );
        const citationPopupCloseBtns = document.getElementsByClassName(
            "citationPopupCloseBtns",
        );
        const citationPopupBackdrops = document.getElementsByClassName(
            "citationPopupBackdrops",
        );

        for (let i = 0; i < citationPopupContainers.length; i++) {
            console.log(
                document.getElementById(`citationPopupContainer-${i + 1}`),
            );

            document
                .getElementById(`citationSuperText-${i + 1}`)
                ?.addEventListener("click", () => {
                    (
                        document.getElementById(
                            `citationPopupContainer-${i + 1}`,
                        ) as HTMLElement
                    ).style.display = "block";
                });

            citationPopupCloseBtns[i]?.addEventListener("click", () => {
                (
                    document.getElementById(
                        `citationPopupContainer-${i + 1}`,
                    ) as HTMLElement
                ).style.display = "none";
            });

            citationPopupBackdrops[i]?.addEventListener("click", () => {
                (
                    document.getElementById(
                        `citationPopupContainer-${i + 1}`,
                    ) as HTMLElement
                ).style.display = "none";
            });
        }
    </script>
</MainLayout>
